<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oirats</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Oirat</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Oirats are a group of western Mongol peoples who became a major power on the Mongolian and Central Asian steppe from the fifteenth century. They raided the eastern lands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moghulistan">Moghulistan</a>, the successor state of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chagatai-khanate">Chagatai Empire</a>. Their pressure contributed to the decline of the Chagatai khans.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/oirats.jpg" alt="Oirats" width="320" height="383" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bukar', Michail · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bukar%27,_Michail_-_Ehepaar_aus_dem_Volksstamm_der_Kalmyken_in_ihrer_Nationaltracht_(Zeno_Fotografie).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
